    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Archivist of the Fracture.</strong> You don’t just survive anomalies—you take notes.</p><ul><li>When your party completes an encounter, operation, or travel segment involving <strong>Sparks, Tikkun events, Qliphothic anomalies, or heavy hex-tilt</strong>, and you had meaningful time to observe or interact with the phenomenon, you can perform a <strong>post-event analysis</strong>.</li><li>On a successful <strong>Occult (Mind), Lore (Mind), or Investigation (Mind)</strong> check (DC set by the GM), your faction gains a small narrative resource bump: extra <strong>intel, research progress, or a +1 OP-equivalent</strong> bonus toward future operations involving that same phenomenon or faction.</li></ul><p>Mechanically, this is your hook for “we learn from weirdness” effects: scripts can look for this flag and award small, repeatable advantages on follow-up rolls.</p>",
